  "description": "Reads Markdown into a DocWright Word document and writes a Word document as Markdown, with no third-party dependencies: CommonMark 0.31.2 plus GitHub's tables, strikethrough and task lists. Headings, code and quotes arrive as real Word styles; images are never fetched; the writer's bullet, emphasis, table and heading spellings are configurable. Export is lossy by nature, because Markdown cannot express fonts, page setup, footnotes or shapes. Most users should install the DocWright package instead, which includes this one.",
